WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:09.200
Element 113 is, again, labelled with this
new systematic

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.540
method for the artificial elements. So you
have un-un-trium

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:22.400
or it might be ununtrium, I don’t know,
which stands for 113.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.519
And you might actually ask, ‘Why should
anybody want to

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:32.980
make a few atoms of these artificial elements?’
And I think

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.970
the answer, I don’t know definitely, is
that there have been

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.470
predictions that although the elements at
this part of the

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:47.300
periodic table are very unstable, that there
may, at heavier

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.320
elements, be one or two elements which are
surprisingly

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.640
stable, might last for very much longer. They
are called

00:00:55.640 --> 00:01:00.170
‘islands of stability’ that have been
predicted, and so people

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.700
are working systematically to see whether
in fact there are

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.470
one or two elements that are in fact really
quite stable even

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:10.690
though they are super heavy. And when I was
a young

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:14.870
researcher in the 1970s, somebody, I can’t
remember who it

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:19.170
was, got very excited because they thought
in remnants of

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:23.900
very ancient mineral mica, it’s a sort of
mineral that comes

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.140
in layers, that they found some strange patterns,
which they

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.620
thought was an indication of super heavy elements
decaying,

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:37.530
perhaps as heavy as element 164. Enormously
heavier than

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.910
anything anybody has been able to create in
the lab. It turned

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.840
out not to be as exciting as they thought
and there was some

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.200
other completely different explanation. But
it is testing

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.820
theories and things like that that really
move science forward.

